diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..15430e0 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,37 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## SMS sign-up verification
+
+Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and set `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`,
+and `TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER` to an SMS-capable Twilio sender. For deployed builds,
+provide these as server environment variables. Credentials stay on the server.
+The integration uses the [Twilio Messages API](https://www.twilio.com/docs/messaging/api/message-resource).
+Without configuration, sending a code returns a clear unavailable message; no
+test code or simulated verification is exposed to users.
+
+Sign-up sends a random six-digit code, verifies it on the server, then permits
+account registration through the existing registration service. Codes expire
+after five minutes, allow five guesses, and are consumed after verification and
+successful registration. Resending replaces the previous challenge, with a
+60-second cooldown and a limit of five sends per phone per hour.
+
+SMS messages end with `@hostname #123456`, using the current request hostname
+without a scheme, port, or path. Use HTTPS and serve the application through a
+trusted host/proxy configuration in production. WebOTP listens before sending
+the SMS and automatically fills and submits the single code input. Browsers
+without WebOTP retain `autocomplete="one-time-code"`, pasting, and manual entry.
+If the browser denies SMS access, users can still enter their code.
+
+Challenge state and per-phone rate limits are held in this Node process and
+bound to the Astro server session. A restart requires a fresh code. Before
+running multiple instances, move challenge state, atomic consumption, and rate
+limits to a shared store and use a shared Astro session driver. Add deployment
+level IP/global SMS quotas to control sending across different phone numbers.
+The external registration API is outside this repository; enforcing this
+verification policy across every client also requires that API to accept only
+trusted server registrations and persist the verified phone association.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for server verification tests (mocked SMS and registration; no
+real messages are sent), and `pnpm build` to validate the application build.
